<section class="panel" aria-label="Grade 3 Unit 8 Lesson 2 first-party number line lesson">
<h2>Create Your Own Number Line</h2>
<p><a href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-8/lesson-2/lesson.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original 2021 teacher activity, including the four visual warm-up prompts</a>. The original student PDF and picture pixels have not been individually inspected.</p>
<p>With three or four classmates, use tape and a marker to draw a floor number line with equal unit intervals from 0 to at least 4. Label <strong>13 source fractions</strong>: 1/2, 1/3, 6/2, 12/3, 1/4, 5/4, 6/6, 5/6, 9/8, 15/8, 5/3, 18/6, 2/8. Some fractions coincide: 1/4=2/8 and 6/2=18/6.</p>
<p>Create six mathematically true comparisons based on your constructed line: two with &lt;, two with =, two with &gt;. Select two to explain using a drawing, numbers or words. Do not treat the first-party examples as the only possible answers.</p>
<p><strong>Teacher review:</strong> verify original warm-up illustrations, physical intervals, fractions at whole-number positions, six correct comparisons and two reasoned explanations. Original publisher Cool-down is not reproduced.</p>
</section>
